    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "Findings on his physical examination were normal except for an exaggerated lordosis with tense contracture of his prominent paraspinal muscles. Magnetic resonance imaging of the head and spinal cord was normal. His complete blood cell count, erythrocyte sedimentation rate, and serum glucose, triiodothyronine, thyroxine, thyroid-stimulating hormone, and cortisol levels were within normal limits. An electromyogram revealed the presence of persistent motor unit potentials in both agonist and antagonist muscles despite the patient's intention to relax, consistent with the diagnosis of SMS. Furthermore, a serum anti-GAD antibody assay was positive.",
      "quote": "Findings on his physical examination were normal except for an exaggerated lordosis with tense contracture of his prominent paraspinal muscles. Magnetic resonance imaging of the head and spinal cord was normal. His complete blood cell count, erythrocyte sedimentation rate, and serum glucose, triiodothyronine, thyroxine, thyroid-stimulating hormone, and cortisol levels were within normal limits. An electromyogram revealed the presence of persistent motor unit potentials in both agonist and antagonist muscles despite the patient's intention to relax, consistent with the diagnosis of SMS. Furthermore, a serum anti-GAD antibody assay was positive.",
      "confidence": "high"
